---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Update an asset" currentPath="/ai-guide/update">
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">AI guide</p>
    <h1>Update an existing asset.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Change one thing. Name exactly what it is. Say explicitly what stays the same. That's the whole discipline.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="body-section">
    <p>Updating is not regenerating. When you update, something already exists and most of it should stay exactly as it is. The more precisely you scope the change, the less the AI touches things you didn't ask about.</p>
    <p>Brandforge stays connected throughout — you don't re-explain the brand or paste anything in. What you bring is the one thing Brandforge can't know: why this change is happening and what the new direction is.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="notice-block">
    <strong>Before you start</strong>
    <p>Open Claude Code with the Metanoia repo connected. You'll use the Read command to load the asset file — the AI sees the current file and Brandforge's rules at the same time, automatically. Don't copy-paste code into the conversation. That creates a disconnected copy. Always load through the repo.</p>
  </div>

  <section class="read-section">
    <h2>Using the Read command</h2>
    <p class="section-intro">The Read command loads any file from the repo into your session. You type it directly in the Claude Code conversation, just like a message.</p>
    <div class="read-walkthrough">
      <div class="read-step">
        <div class="read-step-num">1</div>
        <div class="read-step-body">
          <p>Find the file path in your repo — for example, a landing page lives at <code>site/landing/aic-product.html</code></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="read-step">
        <div class="read-step-num">2</div>
        <div class="read-step-body">
          <p>Type the Read command in your Claude Code conversation:</p>
          <pre><code>Read site/landing/aic-product.html</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="read-step">
        <div class="read-step-num">3</div>
        <div class="read-step-body">
          <p>Claude will confirm the file loaded and summarise what it sees. You'll know it worked when it describes the current content back to you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="read-step">
        <div class="read-step-num">4</div>
        <div class="read-step-body">
          <p>Follow your Read command with your update instruction in the same message or the next one:</p>
          <pre><code>Read site/landing/aic-product.html

Change the headline to "Clarity through structure." Keep the same size, weight, and color — only the words change.</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="steps-section">
    <h2>How to prompt an update</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li class="step">
        <div class="step-num">1</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Load the asset with Read</h3>
          <p>Type <code>Read [file path]</code> to pull the file into context. The AI sees the current asset and Brandforge's rules simultaneously. No setup needed on your end.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <div class="step-num">2</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Name exactly what changes</h3>
          <p>Be specific. Vague instructions give the AI room to interpret — and it will use that room. Precise instructions leave no space for guessing.</p>
          <div class="example-prompt">
            <em>"Change the headline to 'Clarity through structure.' Keep the same size, weight, and color as the current headline — only the words change."</em>
          </div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <div class="step-num">3</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Name what stays the same</h3>
          <p>This is the most important habit in updating. Telling the AI what not to touch is as important as telling it what to change.</p>
          <div class="example-prompt">
            <em>"Update the background color only — don't touch the typography, spacing, or layout."</em>
            <em>"Change the copy only. No visual changes at all."</em>
          </div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <div class="step-num">4</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Verify what moved</h3>
          <p>Ask the AI to confirm what changed before accepting anything. One thing should have moved. Everything else should be identical.</p>
          <div class="example-prompt">
            <em>"Show me only what changed. Confirm everything else is identical to the original file."</em>
          </div>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="step">
        <div class="step-num">5</div>
        <div class="step-body">
          <h3>Push your work</h3>
          <p>When the update is right, use the push command for this surface type to send the change to its destination. Until you push, the update only exists in your session.</p>
          <pre><code># For a landing page:
/push-to-lab</code></pre>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="antipatterns-section">
    <h2>What not to do</h2>
    <ul class="antipatterns-list">
      <li>Paste existing code or CSS into the chat. Use <code>Read</code> instead — pasting creates a disconnected copy that's no longer wired to the real brand.</li>
      <li>Say "make it look better." Name the specific property you want to change. Subjective prompts produce unpredictable output.</li>
      <li>Ask for a redesign when you want a tweak. "Redesign this section" gives the AI permission to rebuild from scratch. Name the one thing.</li>
      <li>Close the session before pushing. Use the push command first — unpushed work disappears when the session ends.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-8);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-size: var(--fs-12);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-wide);
    color: var(--fg-accent);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: var(--fs-36);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-tight);
    line-height: var(--lh-tight);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    color: var(--fg-1);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: var(--fs-18);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    max-width: 580px;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .body-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .body-section p {
    font-size: var(--fs-16);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .body-section p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .notice-block {
    background: var(--bg-accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }
  .notice-block strong {
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    color: var(--fg-accent);
  }
  .notice-block p {
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .notice-block code { font-size: var(--fs-13); color: var(--fg-accent); }

  section { margin-bottom: var(--space-16); }

  h2 {
    font-size: var(--fs-24);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-snug);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
    color: var(--fg-1);
  }

  .section-intro {
    font-size: var(--fs-15);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
    max-width: 560px;
  }

  .read-walkthrough {
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  .read-step {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .read-step-num {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 28px; height: 28px;
    background: var(--bg-accent-soft);
    color: var(--fg-accent);
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: var(--fs-13);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .read-step-body p {
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .read-step-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .read-step-body code { font-size: var(--fs-13); color: var(--fg-accent); }
  .read-step-body pre { margin: var(--space-2) 0 0; }

  .steps { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-6); }

  .step { display: flex; gap: var(--space-5); align-items: flex-start; }

  .step-num {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 32px; height: 32px;
    background: var(--bg-accent-soft);
    color: var(--fg-accent);
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    font-weight: var(--fw-bold);
    margin-top: 2px;
  }

  .step-body h3 {
    font-size: var(--fs-16);
    font-weight: var(--fw-semibold);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
    color: var(--fg-1);
  }

  .step-body p {
    font-size: var(--fs-15);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .step-body p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .step-body code { font-size: var(--fs-13); color: var(--fg-accent); }
  .step-body pre { margin-top: var(--space-3); }

  .example-prompt {
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    font-size: var(--fs-14);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .antipatterns-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .antipatterns-list li {
    font-size: var(--fs-15);
    color: var(--fg-2);
    line-height: var(--lh-relaxed);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }

  .antipatterns-list li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .antipatterns-list code { font-size: var(--fs-13); color: var(--fg-accent); }
</style>
